---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {sources} from '../lib/cars';
---
<Base title="Code reference sources and attribution" description="The community reference datasets and manufacturer documents cited by ErrHive Cars, with provenance labels and licenses." breadcrumbs={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Sources'}]}><article class="container prose-page"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">TRACE THE REFERENCE</p><h1>Sources and attribution.</h1><p class="lede">A community reference definition and a manufacturer diagnostic procedure are different kinds of evidence. Each page identifies the material behind it.</p></header><div class="notice"><p>Imported dataset entries are reference material. Their presence does not establish manufacturer verification, vehicle compatibility, or a confirmed repair.</p></div><ol class="source-list section">{sources.map(source=><li id={source.id}><h2><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.title}</a></h2><p>{source.publisher} · {source.kind==='dataset'?'Community reference dataset':source.kind==='manufacturer'?'Manufacturer document':'Public-agency material'} · Checked {source.checkedOn}</p>{source.license&&<p>Reference license: {source.license}</p>}</li>)}</ol>{!sources.length&&<p class="empty-state">Source records will appear with the first published references.</p>}<p><a href="/research-methodology/">How sources are used</a></p></article></Base>
